From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:28:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] avutil/hwcontext_v4l2request: only enforce the maximum
 frame size

Frames smaller than the minimum of a stepwise ENUM_FRAMESIZES range
were rejected, although S_FMT rounds the buffers up and the smaller
frame decodes fine into them (as GStreamer relies on). Only keep the
maximum as a hard limit.

Fixes the 60 small-size VP9 conformance vectors (vp90-2-02-size-*) on
MediaTek MT8195, whose minimum is 64x64.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c b/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
index a06fc15f90..68e82ec0a8 100644
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
@@ -519,8 +519,11 @@ static int v4l2request_try_framesize(AVHWFramesContext *hwfc,
             return 0;
         } else if ((frmsize.type == V4L2_FRMSIZE_TYPE_STEPWISE ||
                     frmsize.type == V4L2_FRMSIZE_TYPE_CONTINUOUS) &&
-                   hwfc->width >= frmsize.stepwise.min_width &&
-                   hwfc->height >= frmsize.stepwise.min_height &&
+                   /*
+                    * Below the minimum, S_FMT rounds the buffers up and the
+                    * smaller frame still decodes into them; only the maximum
+                    * is a hard limit.
+                    */
                    hwfc->width <= frmsize.stepwise.max_width &&
                    hwfc->height <= frmsize.stepwise.max_height) {
             return 0;
